<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21138] Quota: "Release too much!" on MDT DoM release when a data LQA exists</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21138</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Problem: DoM requests also pull DT LQA pools (qmt_pool.c:415). DoM grant only exists in global dt-0x0; DT LQA lqes are rebuilt from OST slaves, so granted=0 and qmt_lqes_can_rel() rejects the MDT release (-EINVAL).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Release too much! uuid:&amp;lt;fs&amp;gt;-MDT0000-lwp-MDT0000_UUID pool:dt-0x0; real failing entry is next line pool:lqa-dt-* granted:0.
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Repro: quota+DoM; DoM writes as uid; add LQA range for uid (triggers recalc); delete files.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix: skip DT LQA pools for DoM (idx == QMT_POOL_IDX_GLB).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
